+module.exports=[
+ {id:'electricity',slug:'pc-electricity-cost',title:'PC electricity cost calculator',description:'Turn measured wall power, usage time and your electricity rate into a daily, 30-day and annual budget.',answer:'Use measured power at the wall. CPU TDP and graphics-card power ratings are not measurements of a complete PC’s electricity consumption.',fields:[field('watts','Measured power at the wall (W)',200,0,100000),field('hours','Hours used each day',4,0,24),field('rate','Your electricity rate per kWh','',0,100)],notes:['Find the energy charge and currency on your own bill. This tool does not provide a regional tariff. Enter zero deliberately if you are evaluating a zero marginal energy charge; an empty rate is not treated as free electricity.','Formula: watts × daily hours ÷ 1,000 = kWh per day. Multiply by the entered rate. The 30-day and 365-day totals assume the same usage every day. Fixed connection charges, tax and tiered tariffs are excluded unless you account for them yourself.','For a PC with different idle and gaming power, calculate each period separately and add the results. A measured average is more useful than assuming the power supply’s maximum rating is its normal consumption. Include the monitor only if your meter measured it too.']},
+ {id:'platform',slug:'platform-upgrade-cost',title:'Compare complete PC upgrade costs',description:'Compare two CPU-platform budgets, including the board, memory, cooler and other required spending.',answer:'This is a manual budget, not a live store-price comparison. Use the same currency and checkout treatment in both options.',fields:['a','b'].flatMap(key=>['cpu','board','ram','cooler','other'].map(part=>field(key+part,'Option '+key.toUpperCase()+': '+({cpu:'CPU',board:'motherboard',ram:'memory',cooler:'cooling',other:'other required costs'})[part],0,0,1e7))),notes:['Set a reused component to zero only after verifying that its generation, mounting, connections and software requirements fit the new platform. Add shipping, adapters and mounting kits to other required costs where applicable.','Formula: CPU + motherboard + memory + cooling + other costs for each option. Difference = option B minus option A. A positive difference means B costs more; it does not establish which performs better.','Gather exact SKU prices before using this result for a purchase. This calculation does not apply coupons, infer tax rules, or estimate a resale value for your old parts. Use the AM5 checklist and board documentation to resolve compatibility separately.'],related:'/blog/pc-upgrade-total-platform-cost/'},
+ {id:'display',slug:'monitor-pixel-density',title:'Monitor pixel density and size calculator',description:'Calculate pixels per inch and rectangular display dimensions from resolution and diagonal size.',answer:'Pixel density describes the number of pixels per inch. It does not measure contrast, input lag, HDR quality or motion clarity.',fields:[field('x','Horizontal pixels',2560,1,100000,1),field('y','Vertical pixels',1440,1,100000,1),field('diagonal','Display diagonal (inches)',27,.1,1000)],notes:['Formula: PPI = √(horizontal pixels² + vertical pixels²) ÷ diagonal inches. Display width and height use the same resolution aspect ratio and assume square pixels. The result describes the active rectangle, not the stand or full monitor chassis.','Use the panel’s native resolution. Operating-system scaling changes interface size but does not change the physical pixel count. Cropping, unusual pixel geometry or a rounded screen means the computed rectangle is not an exact visible-area measurement.','For a desk layout, confirm the manufacturer’s full dimensions, stand depth and VESA clearance. To evaluate sharpness, consider viewing distance and your own eyesight. The output is geometry, not a recommendation that one PPI is universally best.']},
+ {id:'recording',slug:'recording-storage',title:'Recording storage budget calculator',description:'Estimate storage from a combined video/audio bitrate, recording duration and a manual allowance.',answer:'Use the combined bitrate of the streams you intend to record. Variable-bitrate footage can depart from the chosen average.',fields:[field('bitrate','Combined bitrate (Mb/s)',50,.001,100000),field('hours','Recording duration (hours)',2,0,100000),field('overhead','Extra storage allowance (%)',10,0,1000)],notes:['Formula: Mb/s × 1,000,000 × seconds ÷ 8 = bytes. The extra allowance is then applied. GB uses 1,000,000,000 bytes; GiB uses 1,073,741,824 bytes. Neither number includes editing proxies, backups or operating-system files.','Container overhead and variable scene complexity can change the final file size. Use a short recording at your actual settings to get a better average, and keep a reserve for longer sessions. An encoder quality setting is not necessarily a fixed bitrate.','Drive capacity is only one requirement. Verify sustained write behavior, interface and application requirements separately. Use the storage capacity planner to combine the estimate with your existing files and free-space allowance.']},
+ {id:'ai',slug:'local-ai-memory',title:'Local AI model memory planner',description:'Calculate approximate weight storage and add deliberate budgets for runtime allocations and the KV cache.',answer:'This is a planning lower bound plus your manual allowances. It does not certify that a particular model will load, fit entirely in VRAM or run at a useful speed.',fields:[field('parameters','Parameters (billions)',8,.001,10000),field('bits','Average bits per parameter',4,1,64),field('runtime','Runtime allowance (GiB)','',0,100000),field('kv','KV-cache budget (GiB)','',0,100000)],notes:['Formula: billions of parameters × 1,000,000,000 × average bits ÷ 8 ÷ 2³⁰. Real model files include format details and can mix storage types. Their measured size is stronger evidence than the simplified weight calculation.','Enter runtime and cache budgets from the configuration you plan to use. Empty values are unresolved, not zero. Context length, concurrency and cache format matter, so this tool does not infer the cache from token count alone.','Confirm software support and record actual peak memory and response speed with a representative prompt before purchasing hardware. CPU offloading, GPU memory and system RAM are separate resources, not a single guaranteed pool.'],related:'/blog/local-ai-memory-weights-kv-cache/'},
+ {id:'frametime',slug:'frame-time-budget',title:'FPS and refresh interval calculator',description:'Translate FPS and display refresh rate into milliseconds per frame and refresh interval.',answer:'This translates rates into intervals. It does not predict your PC’s FPS or measure input latency.',fields:[field('fps','Frame rate (FPS)',60,.1,10000),field('hz','Display refresh rate (Hz)',144,.1,10000)],notes:['Formula: 1,000 ÷ FPS = milliseconds per frame. The same reciprocal calculation gives the refresh interval from Hz. A 60 FPS rate corresponds to 16.67 ms per frame; 120 FPS corresponds to 8.33 ms.','An average FPS value is not evidence that every frame took that interval. A frame-time trace is needed to describe spikes and consistency. Generated frames, rendering cadence and input sampling also should not be collapsed into one latency number.','Use the interval to understand a performance target or compare units in a review. It does not establish a frame cap, synchronization configuration or hardware purchase recommendation. The site’s separate PC FPS model remains unvalidated.']},
+ {id:'lanes',slug:'b650-tomahawk-lane-check',title:'B650 TOMAHAWK slot-sharing checker',description:'Check the documented M2_3/PCI_E2 rule and the Ryzen 8500/8300 restriction on M2_2.',answer:'This tool applies only to MAG B650 TOMAHAWK WIFI. It is not a general B650 or AM5 compatibility engine.',fields:[],notes:['Select which two shared connections are occupied. PCI_E2 is listed at up to PCIe 4.0 ×2. M2_3 is listed at ×4 by itself, changing to ×2 when both are occupied. The output describes a link, not a benchmark result.','MSI also states that M2_2 is unavailable with Ryzen 8500 and 8300 processors. The CPU-group control reflects that restriction. It does not replace checking the exact supported processor and BIOS version.','Check the printed labels on your board and follow the manual before moving devices. Do not apply this topology to another motherboard with similar slot names. The companion article explains how to keep a useful build record.'],sources:['msi'],related:'/blog/b650-tomahawk-m2-pcie-lane-sharing/'}
