+md('20-discover-implementation.md',`## Shipped\n16 original 1200 × 675 explanatory PNGs, plus the software-guide diagram. New articles/tools use representative Open Graph imagery and max-image-preview:large. No fake product photographs or stock benchmark charts were created. Normal canonical sitemap and crawlable links include substantive new pages.\n\n## Editorial checks\nVerify a large image is relevant and legible, not merely a logo. These diagrams are allowed explanatory artwork, not evidence of a hardware test. Check image compression and actual field loading behavior after deployment. Large images and indexing do not guarantee Discover traffic.\n\n## Preferred Sources\nGoogle’s September 2026 documentation requires the domain/subdomain to appear in its source-preference search. Eligibility for this site is unverified, so a promotional button is not installed. Owner can check the domain at https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=pcpartperformance.com. Do not change the owner’s Google preferences as an eligibility test.\n\n## Search profile investigation\nGoogle currently lists US availability and a 10,000-follower minimum on a supported platform, plus account/policy requirements. This user’s eligibility and connected creator accounts are unknown. No profile was claimed or fabricated. Google says profile creation does not directly change ranking.\n\nSources: ${sources.discover.url}, ${sources.preferred.url}, ${sources.profile.url}`);
+md('21-ad-revenue-plan.md',`## Default-off implementation\nAd configuration lives in scripts/ad-policy.cjs. enabled=false, publisherApproved=false, no publisher ID and cmpVerified=false. No ad scripts or empty ad boxes are rendered. A gate also requires consent and respects GPC; it excludes builder, comparison, FPS, phone-size and search interactions. This gate is not a complete CMP or legal-compliance claim.\n\n## Prerequisites\nVerified AdSense publisher account and site approval; Google-certified CMP where required; a region-aware consent policy; actual privacy/contact/controller details; current ads.txt values supplied by the account. Do not invent an ads.txt authorization. Audit existing Google Fonts requests and remote 3D dependencies before making any no-third-party-request statement.\n\n## Placements\nStart with article-end context. Consider a single reserved mid-article placement only after evidence of stable layout and engagement. No overlays, sticky ads near pickers, mislabeled buttons or ad-driven form delays. Disclose sponsorship/affiliate relationships next to their content and use appropriate paid-link attributes.\n\n## Privacy review\nCanadian behavioural-advertising guidance treats tracking as generally involving personal information and describes consent conditions. California rules apply to covered businesses and include GPC obligations. Determine actual applicability with the owner’s business facts and counsel; no universal compliance guarantee is made.\n\nSources: ${sources.ads.url}; ${sources.opc.url}; ${sources.ccpa.url}`);
+md('23-phone-vertical-plan.md',`## Decision\nLaunch a small specification/tool cohort, not a generic phone-news division or newest-phone ranking. The current catalog already includes phones; a first-party comparison question supports qualitative interest, not a volume estimate. Manufacturer dimensions create an original same-scale tool without a test lab.\n\n## Implemented\nFive records; two focused comparisons; same-scale size overlay; policy-evidence tracker; per-field null/source/check/confidence. Exact regional SIM/network fields and fixed support end dates are held.\n\n## Hold\nBattery/camera winners, repairability scores, charging speed predictions, newest-generation recommendations and live offers require verified source data or original tests. A charger checker needs exact protocol/cable/adapter contracts; it is not reduced to wattage.\n\n## Growth gate\nUse Search Console and real support questions to justify additions, then source each model/region. Do not generate every phone pairing.\n\nDemand proxy (nonrepresentative): ${sources.demandphones.url}`);
+md('24-phone-data-schema.md',`Schema v1: {id, name, region, verified, fields, support}. Every field is {value, source, checked, confidence}; missing values are null with confidence=not verified. Support preserves commitment, starting-event description, exact endDate and policy source separately.\n\nFields include body height/width/depth/weight, diagonal/resolution/SoC/storage, RAM and typical battery where checked. Regional model number, launch/current OS, measured battery/brightness/charging, repairability, SIM, connectivity, camera testing and prices are nullable slots. A populated nullable schema is not a claim that all requested evidence is available.\n\nSources and regions: Apple published specifications; Google UK cohort; Samsung Canada cohort. Values are not merged across regional models. Support end dates stay null. Never sort null as zero.\n\nRuntime dataset: /data/phones-v1.json and /api/v1/phones.json. Source module: scripts/phone-data.cjs.`);
+md('25-phone-comparison-template.md',`One clear title, scope description, table of verified fields, links to both source records, same-scale size-tool action and update-policy action. Unknown cells read Not verified. No composite winner score.\n\nCompare body dimensions before chip names. Explain that dimensions do not certify grip, camera bump or case fit. Typical battery capacity does not establish endurance; chip names do not establish sustained speed. Keep product region and storage code separate from generic family names.\n\nOnly two curated stable routes shipped. Arbitrary filter/search states are not generated as indexed pages. A future tested comparison must record test conditions and distinguish measured data from manufacturer specifications.`);
+md('26-video-youtube-system.md',`## Verified resource\nNVIDIA GeForce: RTX 50-series announcement; January 7, 2025; ${sources.video.url}. Source search metadata identified the verified channel and title; duration is unrecorded. Scope is the whole family and company presentation, not an exact partner-card test.\n\n## Implementation\n/resources/ supplies a clearly labeled external video action and written context. No autoplay, iframe, thumbnail tracking request or VideoObject claim. A link-only resource is not the primary watch page.\n\n## Registry contract\nStore videoId, URL, title, creator, verification date, upload date, model scope, purpose, duration if verified, accessibility/transcript availability and source/license notes. Recheck broken links without replacing the written explanation. Only a genuine primary watch page with prominent playable media and complete matching metadata should be considered for VideoObject. Creator ownership and publication details must be real.`);
+md('31-retention-strategy.md',`Implemented local saved list for products/new guides/tools/phones, capped at 100 IDs. No account, email, cross-device sync, price tracking or alerts. Safe text rendering and canonical result URLs; storage errors produce a message. Local search fetches a small index on demand and normalizes model aliases; no raw query is transmitted to analytics.\n\nTwo existing subscriptions: Blog RSS (evergreen articles) and News RSS (currently empty because no approved news). Do not mix evergreen preparation dates into fresh news.\n\nNewsletter, email alerts and cloud watchlists remain disabled until the owner selects a service, sender identity, consent/unsubscribe process and privacy policy. No form pretends to subscribe someone. Saved-list export is a next step, with import validation and explicit merge rules. Measure returning use only after a consented analytics property exists.`);
+md('32-revenue-dashboard-spec.md',`## No baseline connected\nNo AdSense, affiliate, analytics or Search Console account data is available. All revenue/traffic fields are null, not zero.\n\n## Metrics\nBy canonical page group, country, device and date: estimated new/returning active users, engaged sessions, tool success, article engagement, qualified retailer clicks, actual ad impressions, viewability, revenue, page RPM, affiliate confirmed conversions, field CLS/INP/LCP. Page RPM = revenue / page views × 1000; session RPM uses sessions, with an explicit denominator. Never treat a click as a sale.\n\n## Joins and consent\nJoin aggregate canonical-path/day/country/device data rather than identities. Strip queries/build lists. No raw search terms, emails, IPs or cross-site identifiers in events. Respect consent withdrawal and GPC where applicable. Exclude preview/staff traffic.\n\n## Decision rule\nCompare date-aligned periods and confidence/sample size. Do not extrapolate an RPM from another publisher. A placement ships only after revenue and engagement are measured with stable field performance. Property credentials/export permissions are the blocker, not a missing chart.`);
+md('33-content-freshness-system.md',`Research dates are preserved in publication metadata and source records. Stage 2 datePublished is null until confirmed hosting; source-check dates do not masquerade as publication. Evergreen modification dates change for material text/evidence edits. Existing Stage 1 dates were preserved.\n\nRun scripts/audit-publication-freshness.cjs to compare source/content hashes against its previous audit and list review dates. It reports changes; it does not rewrite dates, publish a story or retitle it latest.\n\nQuarterly evergreen check; monthly support/market policy check; event-driven release review. A scheduled cloud monitor is not active. Once a hosting source/automation list is verified, reuse its existing schedule or configure an owner-approved one. Intake is a draft signal, not autopublishing.`);
+md('34-source-confidence-system.md',`Classify each claim: manufacturer specification; independently measured with identified setup; site calculation with explicit inputs; company forecast; inherited unverified field; unavailable. Primary status establishes source origin, not truth beyond its scope.\n\nThe phone dataset stores this per field. Board checker points to the exact MSI document. Catalog audit says field coverage is not correctness. Community questions only motivate research; they never validate specifications or demand volume.\n\nIf sources disagree, retain both citations, model/region/revision and an unresolved note. Stop the affected recommendation rather than average conflicting values. Correction review must trace all affected comparisons.`);
+md('35-data-changelog-system.md',`Public /data/changelog/ records the prepared release, additions, coverage version and unresolved fields. It does not claim confirmed live deployment. Future entries identify old/new value, source URL/date, affected model IDs/pages, reviewer role and material reason.\n\nPreserve old dataset versions when public consumers need reproducibility. A rebuild or source availability check is not a substantive revision. Unknown publication dates remain unknown. Support end-date additions require anchor evidence. Exact-photo corrections require actual identity verification, not a relabeled family image.`);
+md('36-public-dataset-plan.md',`Shipped site-authored aggregate category/field/image counts in hashed CSV/JSON, plus schema-versioned phone JSON. No full photo/model asset redistribution. CC0 applies only to authored aggregate counts, not third-party images, models or an entire copied catalog.\n\nReport denominator=unique local IDs, snapshot date, formulas, hash and limitations. Counts are not representative of market share or demand. For future change reports, preserve both snapshots and disclose catalog additions that changed the denominator.\n\nRetail time series and frame-time datasets wait for permitted sourcing and reproducible observations. Do not infer stock or benchmark samples from existing specification records.`);
+md('37-api-plan.md',`Static public /api/v1/catalog-coverage.json and /api/v1/phones.json are usable fetch endpoints today in the local build. They return snapshots, not prices.\n\nOptional scripts/public-data-api.cjs exposes extensionless GET/HEAD paths, hardcoded datasets, ETag/304 handling, 15-minute file cache, 60/minute per direct address, bounded in-memory client state and nosniff. Unknown routes=404; unsupported methods=405; limit=429 with Retry-After; unavailable file=503. No arbitrary path/URL fetching.\n\nThis adapter is tested but not attached to the static Sites host. Production requires a compatible server runtime and proxy-aware trusted-client policy, shared rate limits across instances, access logs with privacy retention rules and monitoring. Static endpoints do not enforce the Node limit. No API key is needed for public nonpersonal snapshots; private data is outside the contract.`);
+md('38-release-calendar-plan.md',`No release-calendar dates were guessed from rumors. Proposed schema: exact product/software ID, event kind (announcement/availability/update), region, confirmed date or null, timezone, source URL/check date, confidence and revision history.\n\nOnly manufacturer-confirmed dates enter a public calendar. Keep a withdrawn date visible with a correction, not a silently moved event. An availability date differs from announcement and order date. Historical dates can support context but do not create fresh news.\n\nIntake can queue candidates; editors verify the original document. Release alerts require an actual subscription service and consent. Until enough verified upcoming events exist, no thin calendar hub is indexed.`);
+md('39-memory-market-watch.md',`Completed /blog/memory-market-watch-ai-is-not-a-retail-price/ separates Micron’s dated company AI-demand report from desktop-kit prices. A separate unpublished news draft records the missing independent market evidence.\n\nNo retail trend is claimed. To build one, specify stores, exact SKU/kit count/capacity/timings, seller/condition, observed currency/time, stock, tax and shipping. Define how unavailable listings and variant mismatches are treated. Repeated consistent observations are required; search snippets are not a live quote feed.\n\nPublication threshold: dated source + original desktop relevance + transparent sampling. Do not use financial guidance as proof of a consumer shortage or a predicted price jump. Source: ${sources.micron.url}`);
+md('45-stage2-status-and-blockers.md',`## Completed locally\n${manifest.newPages.length} new pages; ${pages.length} sourced full guides; ${tools.length} calculators; five phone records; two comparisons; a size overlay/support tracker; original aggregate report/API snapshots; local search/saved list; source registry; news intake and publication gates; default-off ad policy.\n\n216 scoped source-backed opportunities, 50-entry mixed publishing queue, 100 additional article concepts and 32 original feature briefs. These are researched problem scopes, not 216 measured-demand analyses or published pages. No keyword volumes were invented.\n\n## Blockers\n- Sites native get_site/source credential/save/deploy/status tools unavailable in this task. Existing project ID appgprj_6aa9c3ce35e08191a97584ffe0372d4e is preserved. No deployment success or live-domain update can be claimed.\n- No verified hosting source/linked automation list, so no cloud source-monitor schedule was activated. CLI intake works.\n- AdSense approval/publisher ID, actual CMP, legal/business policy facts and ads.txt values missing. Ads stay off.\n- Search Console/analytics/revenue accounts missing; no traffic, ranking, revenue or field CWV uplift measured.\n- Search profile/Preferred Sources eligibility and creator account access unverified; no application or button claim.\n- Independent test equipment/data and many exact regional/photo/model fields missing. No false certification or measured-phone/AI/gaming claims.\n- Authorized live retailer offers and historical observations unavailable; no prices invented.\n\nNo promise of continuing asynchronously is made. The queue is available for the next explicitly run review.`);
